  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal contract obligations in Rhode Island total $563M, with 3,587 awards and an average award size of $157K. Obligations are down 38.0% year over year and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, accounting for $455M of obligations. Outside the DoD, the Department of Veterans Affairs and Department of Homeland Security are the next-largest agencies, at $50.3M and $16.5M respectively. Leading vendors include RAYTHEON COMPANY at $80.3M and SEACORP, LLC at $56.3M. Engineering Services is the largest industry by obligations at $198M, followed by Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $71.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $43.8M. The distribution of obligations shows heavy concentration in defense-related buying and industries, with construction, remediation, and several manufacturing NAICS also represented in the top ten.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal contracting in Rhode Island?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense drives most contracting with $455M in obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $50.3M, and the Department of Homeland Security is third at $16.5M. Other notable buyers include the General Services Administration at $11.3M and the Department of Labor at $7.6M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries capture the most obligations?",
        "body": "RAYTHEON COMPANY is the largest vendor at $80.3M, followed by SEACORP, LLC at $56.3M and RITE-SOLUTIONS, INC. at $45M. Engineering Services is the top industry with $198M in obligations, with Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $71.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $43.8M also in the top three."
      }
    ]
  },
